1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,479
Yesterday I told you: once the water goes in, the clock starts.

2
00:00:04,479 --> 00:00:05,429
Here's why.

3
00:00:05,429 --> 00:00:08,971
Inside that vial, the peptide is a dry powder.

4
00:00:08,971 --> 00:00:10,026
Freeze-dried.

5
00:00:10,026 --> 00:00:11,523
Almost nothing moves.

6
00:00:11,523 --> 00:00:13,893
No water, no reactions.

7
00:00:13,893 --> 00:00:15,755
The molecule is on pause.

8
00:00:15,755 --> 00:00:17,148
Then water goes in.

9
00:00:17,148 --> 00:00:18,736
And everything changes.

10
00:00:18,736 --> 00:00:23,880
The molecules can move again, and the chemistry that water enables comes back with them.

11
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:27,187
Dry powder and solution are two different worlds.

12
00:00:27,187 --> 00:00:28,619
One is built to wait.

13
00:00:28,619 --> 00:00:30,260
One is built to be used.

14
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:32,291
That was the moment the clock started.

15
00:00:32,291 --> 00:00:33,489
But here's the thing.

16
00:00:33,489 --> 00:00:35,143
There isn't just one clock.

17
00:00:35,143 --> 00:00:36,236
That's tomorrow.

18
00:00:36,236 --> 00:00:37,408
Day one of ten.

19
00:00:37,408 --> 00:00:38,723
The clock is running.

20
00:00:38,723 --> 00:00:40,598
Follow so you don't miss day two.

